      "title": "Qt: Make it a little easier to drag the comment axis",
      "message": "Qt: Make it a little easier to drag the comment axis\n\nDon't require a two stage process. Hightlight the axis while dragging.\n\nSet the Comment axis tick length to zero, so ticks don't display\nwhile the axis is selected. The QCP documentation for setTicks\nclaims \"Note that setting show to false does not imply that tick\nlabels are invisible, too,\" but in practice setting it to false does\nmake the labels invisible. A length 0 does what we want.\n\nSet the cursor shapes to hint that dragging a splitter is possible.\n\nAllow double-clicks anywhere on the axis to widen it automatically\nto the full label length.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2024-07-02T08:01:55.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
